org/10.23668/psycharchives.4988"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"In two samples (213 university students and 470 members of the Austrian public), we assessed the prevalence and psychological correlates of sexuality myth endorsement. Here, we shared anonymized data and the code to reproduce all results reported in our manuscript.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"Table of contents of the ZIP: parent folder: Analyses.Rproj - the R-Project; Study1_SexMyths_analyses.rmd / .pdf -\u0026gt; syntax / output for Study 1; Study2_SexMyths_analyses.rmd / .pdf -\u0026gt; syntax / output for Study 2; BothSamples_SexMyths_analyses.rmd / .pdf -\u0026gt; syntax / output for some comparisons between the studies; this readme. Data (We are sharing all data as .RData and .csv.): SexMythsItems_GerEn_corrected.csv/.xlsx - a list of all sex myths items, to be read into R in the .rmd files; Study1_demographics.csv/.RData - demographic data for Study 1 (stored separately for anonymization); Study1_researchdata.csv/.RData - main raw research data for Study 1; Study1_cleandata.csv/.RData - preprocessed data for Study 1 (documented in the .rmd); Study2_researchdata.csv/.RData - full raw research data for Study 2 (apart from open text responses to demographics); Study2_cleandata.csv/.RData - preprocessed data for Study 2 (documented in the .rmd). Documentation: Study 1_Codebook.pdf - Documentation; Study 2_Codebook.pdf - Documentation. Results: SUPP2_Intercorrelations.xlsx and SUPP2_Intercorrelations1/2/3/4.pdf - Large intercorrelation tables that could not automatically be printed into the main .pdf files; after execution of .rmds: outputs for the manuscript.","descriptionType":"TableOfContents"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://www.psycharchives.org/jspui/handle/20.500.12034/18164","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":0,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount"